-- title:
--   Reducedness of the special fibre of a Drinfeld crossing chart
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime number and let $W$ be a local commutative ring whose maximal ideal is principal, generated by an element $\varpi$, and such that the image of $q$ in $W$ lies in the maximal ideal. Let $a \in \mathfrak{m}_W$, and let $f, u, v$ be formal power series in two variables $X_0, X_1$ over $W$ (indexed by `Fin 2`) with $u$ a unit of $W[[X_0,X_1]]$. Assume that $f$ agrees with the Drinfeld form $X_0 X_1^{q} - X_0^{q} X_1$ modulo the $(q+2)$-nd power of the ideal $(X_0, X_1)$, i.e. $f - (X_0X_1^{q} - X_0^{q}X_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$. Then the $W$-algebra
--   $$\kappa \otimes_W \bigl(W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(a)\,v - f\,u)\bigr),$$
--   where $\kappa$ is the residue field of $W$ and $C(a)$ denotes the constant power series with value $a$, is reduced: it has no nonzero nilpotent elements.
--
--   This is the reducedness of the special fibre of the local chart of a Drinfeld modular curve at a crossing point, in the form used for the model of Katz–Mazur: over the residue field the fibre degenerates into the $q+1$ distinct branches cut out by $X_0X_1^{q} - X_0^{q}X_1$. It is the input to the regularity/reducedness statements [`FormalGroup.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic.isReduced_quotient_span_of_isRegularLocalRing_of_pow_sub_one_eq_mul`](thm.html#FormalGroup.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic.isReduced_quotient_span_of_isRegularLocalRing_of_pow_sub_one_eq_mul) and its prime variant, where the equation $C(a)v - fu$ and the congruence on $f$ arise as the normal form of a chart ring.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPowerSeries_isReduced_residueField_tensorProduct_quotient_span_C_mul_sub_mul_of_sub_drinfeldForm_mem_pow.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
